{{Quote|Presenting Borbig Drob the Houk! Nine-time champion of the Stormblade Bloodfest!|An introduction for the Houk gladiator Borbig Drob|<ref name="EG" />}}
'''Houks''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of hulking [[humanoid]]s that had massive [[Limb|forearms]] and were capable of building heavy musculature.

==Biology and appearance==
The Houk were a [[Sentience|sentient]], [[humanoid]] [[species]] distinguished by their muscular bulk, and large [[Limb|arms]]<ref name="EG" /> that ended in four-fingered hands.<ref name="Journal" /> They had tiny [[eye]]s set deep in their thick, [[bone]]-ridged skull.<ref name="SWU">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref>

==History==
A number of [[Houk–Weequay wars|wars]] were waged between members of the Houk race and the [[Weequay]] species.<ref name="Gadgets and Gear">''[[Gadgets and Gear]]''</ref> During the [[Separatist Crisis]], a [[Weequay-Houk brawl|brawl]] erupted between members of the two species.<ref name="Coruscant">{{EncyclopediaCite|Coruscant}}</ref>

==Houks in the galaxy==
[[File:Houk-BountyHunters35.png|thumb|left|200px|A Houk]]
Owing to their powerful builds, Houk [[prisoner]]s were found in large numbers in the [[spice]] [[Spice mines of Kessel|mines]] of [[Kessel]].<ref name="TOG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref>

Some found employment as [[gladiator]]s. During the early [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Era|reign]], [[Borbig Drob]] earned the title of champion at the [[Stormblade Bloodfest]] on nine occasions, before fighting at the [[Gladiator Night]] event on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. There he fought against the [[Feeorin]] gladiator [[Warjak]] before being defeated by the [[Trandoshan]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]].<ref name="EG" /> At some point during the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Unidentified Houk gladiator|another]] Houk fought alongside a [[Kajain'sa'Nikto|Red Nikto]] and a [[Trandoshan]]. Although they had a single opponent, the [[Wookiee]] known as [[Krrsantan]], the Houk and his fighting partners were all killed in the pit.<ref name="Doctor Aphra Annual">[[Doctor Aphra Annual 1|''Doctor Aphra Annual'' 1]]</ref>

Around [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ShadowFallDate}}</ref> the Houk siblings [[Jorgatha]] and [[Gorgeous Su]] served in the [[New Republic]]'s [[61st Mobile Infantry]] on the planet [[Troithe]].<ref name="Shadow Fall">''[[Shadow Fall: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Houk_by_Ezra.png|thumb|right|200px|Borbig Drob]]
The Houk were first created for the [[Star Wars Legends]] novel ''[[Han Solo and the Lost Legacy]]'', which was written by [[Brian Daley]] and released in [[1980]].<ref name="HSLL">''[[Han Solo and the Lost Legacy]]''</ref> Though Daley's novel is now part of the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity rather than the current [[canon]],<ref name="EUNewPage">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> the Houk species was canonized in the [[2014]] junior novel ''[[Ezra's Gamble]]'' by [[Ryder Windham]].<ref name="EG" />

